    "decision_rule": "LOAN_ISSUANCE_PROPERTY bridge rows define eligible NY loans by one origination date, one nonzero rounded amount, at most one originator/originator_match_text, and filed borough. Non-round loans select ACRIS mortgage documents by amount_cents, recorded_date within origination date plus 45 days, and legal_borough equal to filed borough. Round-lattice loans additionally require the lender party role for the document type and party_name_norm equal to originator_match_text. A loan is accepted only when exactly one legal-confirmed ACRIS document remains; truth_bbls are that document's distinct legal BBLs in deterministic order.",
    "proof_boundary": "The retained H.7 truth BBLs are derived from ACRIS legal rows joined on the selected mortgage DOCUMENT_ID. The ACRIS completeness relation is production-relevant evidence but definitional on this population; it must not be cited as independent precision."
